      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4ecad30c",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the East Asian woman as the target of the stereotype",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the East Asian woman (East_Asian_woman) as the subject of the meme's harmful stereotype. The meme implies that she is the one who has 'English tattoos' (text_chunk_2), which is a false and offensive claim. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the projection is implicit: the user is positioned as the one interpreting the meme and thus identifying with the perspective that sees the woman as the object of the stereotype. The user is projected onto the visual material (East_Asian_woman) and the textual material (text_chunk_2) that together form the stereotype.",
